
// 5. Longest Palindromic Substring
// Given a string s, return the longest palindromic substring in s.
// Example 1:

// Input: s = "babad"
// Output: "bab"
// Explanation: "aba" is also a valid answer.
// Example 2:

// Input: s = "cbbd"
// Output: "bb"
 

// Constraints:

// 1 <= s.length <= 1000
// s consist of only digits and English letters.

Brute Force :
1. Generate all substrings
2. Check there are palindorme or not
3. if yes check maxlen and starting index 
4. return s.substring(start , start + maxLen);

Here the time complexity goes to O(n^2) x O(n) ~ O(n^3);

To reduce it : Optimize apporoch is :
Observation is While checking palindrom 
for example : "aaaaaaaaaaaa"
we check recursively from s(0 , 12) -> (1,11) -> (2,10) -> likewise 

so again when we check the for substring of it suppose aaaaaa

in this we have already calculated it in larger one 

So instead of computing it again and again (i.e Overlapping Problems)

we can compute its one and use it again and again 

i.e DP 


class Solution {
    public int isPalindrome(String s , int i , int j , int[][] dp){
        if(i >= j ) return 1;

        if(dp[i][j] != -1 ) return dp[i][j];

        if(s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)) return dp[i][j] = isPalindrome(s,i+1,j-1,dp);

        return dp[i][j] = 0;
    }
    public String longestPalindrome(String s) {
        int n = s.length();
        int maxLen = -1;
        int start = 0;

        int[][] dp = new int[n][n];

        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            Arrays.fill(dp[i] , -1);
        }

        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            for(int j=i ;j<n;j++){
                if(isPalindrome(s , i , j , dp) == 1){
                    if((j-i+1) > maxLen){
                        maxLen = j-i + 1;
                        start = i;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return s.substring(start , start + maxLen);
    }
}